codex
Root cause is now concrete: this audit container’s PID namespace exposes `/proc/self/exe` but not `/proc/<getpid()>/exe`; Lean 4.22 resolves its executable using the unavailable numeric path. I’m applying a narrow process-local compatibility shim that redirects only `/proc/<digits>/exe` `readlink` calls to `/proc/self/exe`, while keeping the pinned direct toolchain first in `PATH`. This does not modify candidate or generated sources.
